(1944424, 265443, 22734, '<td valign="top">Hey Robert: this one really impressed me with the great ise of color. It can certainly bring pride to any wall.</td>', 'Hey Robert: this one really impressed me with the great ise of color. It can certainly bring pride to any wall.', '2005-12-12 11:25:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1944427, 265112, 29269, '<td valign="top">I could not stop laughing when I read your description. I am still chuckling imagining you do it. I don''t think that this "photographer''s rights" paper-printout would have saved you if someone called the authorities on you - it would be the insane asylum people after you, not the DHS.<br/> <br/>Oh, technically it is noce. Crooked horizon spoils it a bit, and I would have preferred to see the open-ended road in the background (if such composition was available to you at the time.) Nice DOF, just the right amount of blur.</td>', 'I could not stop laughing when I read your description. I am still chuckling imagining you do it. I don''t think that this "photographer''s rights" paper-printout would have saved you if someone called the authorities on you - it would be the insane asylum people after you, not the DHS. Oh, technically it is noce. Crooked horizon spoils it a bit, and I would have preferred to see the open-ended road in the background (if such composition was available to you at the time.) Nice DOF, just the right amount of blur.', '2005-12-12 11:26:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1944435, 265208, 22734, '<td valign="top">A very nice presentation and I do follow your thinking. This could have finished much higher by taking advantage of the still life wherein you can place camera on a support and then close the lens all the way down and shoot it at whatever prolonged time you need. You then focus on the tip of the handle. Despite this, the concept was solid and the color selection was on the money.</td>', 'A very nice presentation and I do follow your thinking. This could have finished much higher by taking advantage of the still life wherein you can place camera on a support and then close the lens all the way down and shoot it at whatever prolonged time you need. You then focus on the tip of the handle. Despite this, the concept was solid and the color selection was on the money.', '2005-12-12 11:29:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1944450, 265441, 17203, '<td valign="top">This entry was seriously underrated IMO. I expected a top 10. Maybe shooting from an angle rather than overhead (to show more of the road) would have made the difference.</td>', 'This entry was seriously underrated IMO. I expected a top 10. Maybe shooting from an angle rather than overhead (to show more of the road) would have made the difference.', '2005-12-12 11:37:17.000000', NULL, 0),
